## VOCABULARY
porphyrinoid system, a class of chemical compounds containing four pyrrole units often linked through cyclic arrangement; biomolecules, molecules present or produced by living organisms ranging from small molecules (amino acids, vitamins, neurotransmitters, metabolites) to macromolecules (proteins, carbohydrates, nucleic acids) that play essential roles in biological processes; biosensor, a device that measures biological analytes by generating response that varies with the concentration of the analyte; hybrid materials, physical/ chemical composites made by synergetic combination of organic and inorganic components that influence their physicochemical properties; synergistic combination, a combination where the combined effect is greater than that predicted by their individual potencies; point-of care testing, laboratory testing that provides rapid test results conducted close to the site of patient care with potential for improved patient care; structure−property relationship, a connection that predicts, explains, and controls the behavior and properties of the product in material design and development.
